description:
Quadsat is a high-technology developer specializing in payloads and software solutions for long-range radio-electronic intelligence operations, particularly for the detection and geolocation of radio frequency (RF) emitters across a wide electromagnetic spectrum range.

The SpectraLoc system is a platform-independent airborne payload which, when integrated with UAVs and specialized software, enables the detection and geolocation of radar stations, air defense assets, communication systems, and electronic warfare systems.

Key technical characteristics of SpectraLoc:

• Operating frequency range: 2–18 GHz;
• Wideband spectrum scanning;
• Detection and direction finding of RF emitters at distances up to 150–200 km;
• Target coordinate determination at distances up to 100 km;
• Real-time transmission of intelligence data.

The SpectraLoc payloads combine advanced RF detection with intelligent software to deliver mission-ready electromagnetic warfare (EW) capabilities. These capabilities are vital for gaining tactical and operational superiority in today’s battlefield. 
The SpectraLoc system has already been integrated with the UpTeko LARK multirotor UAV, Skyeton Raybird-3 fixed-wing UAV and test flights and integration with Tekever and other unmanned platforms is also possible.

Located at the UAS Denmark Test Center- one of Europe’s leading drone test centers – at Hans Christian Andersen Airport in Odense.

Visit our booth at the Danish Pavilion, booth no. 7817. 
Meet the team and discover how SpectraLoc can support your operational requirements and strengthen your electromagnetic warfare capabilities.
